WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.027 --> 00:00:04.527
(vibrant xylophone music)

00:00:16.281 --> 00:00:20.353
- When I perform on stage
I'm in my own world.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:21.591
The only thing going through my head

00:00:21.591 --> 00:00:25.758
is that nothing else exists
but the trick I'm doing

00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:29.047
in that current moment,

00:00:29.047 --> 00:00:30.789
and the yo-yo flings up in the air,

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:32.687
goes under my leg, it's being bounced

00:00:32.687 --> 00:00:34.842
back and forth between the strings,

00:00:34.842 --> 00:00:38.202
whipping sideways, horizontally.

00:00:38.202 --> 00:00:40.879
The way I express myself
on stage comes out

00:00:40.879 --> 00:00:45.045
and I love that feeling
where you can kinda be free.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.158
(rhythmic music)

00:00:47.158 --> 00:00:48.363
When I'm not on stage,

00:00:48.363 --> 00:00:51.873
I'm a graphic designer
living in Los Angeles.

00:00:51.873 --> 00:00:55.296
Most of the year I'm just
like any typical recent grad

00:00:55.296 --> 00:00:57.185
trying to figure out what
to do with their life,

00:00:57.185 --> 00:00:59.883
but come summer I'm preparing to be

00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:03.542
the best yo-yo performer
at the World Yo-Yo Contest.

00:01:03.542 --> 00:01:04.619
My name is Ben Conde.

00:01:04.619 --> 00:01:06.411
I am a professional yo-yo player,

00:01:06.411 --> 00:01:08.342
and I'm ranked number one in North America

00:01:08.342 --> 00:01:10.166
in the offstring division.

00:01:10.166 --> 00:01:12.256
(rhythmic drumming)

00:01:12.256 --> 00:01:15.125
I think people think yo-yos
are incredibly simple,

00:01:15.125 --> 00:01:17.854
but it's gone a long way since being

00:01:17.854 --> 00:01:19.220
a toy that goes up and down

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.226
and now there's all
these new elements to it.

00:01:22.226 --> 00:01:24.696
(techno music)

00:01:24.696 --> 00:01:27.778
Many people don't know there
are five styles of yo-yo.

00:01:27.778 --> 00:01:29.581
There's one-handed yo-yo,

00:01:29.581 --> 00:01:32.093
there's two-handed responsive yo-yo,

00:01:32.093 --> 00:01:33.958
two-handed unresponsive yo-yo,

00:01:33.958 --> 00:01:36.466
counterweight yo-yo, and offstring yo-yo,

00:01:36.466 --> 00:01:39.229
which is what I specialize in.

00:01:39.229 --> 00:01:42.141
It's riskier, it's the riskiest
division, in my opinion,

00:01:42.141 --> 00:01:45.532
because of the fact that
it can fall off the string.

00:01:45.532 --> 00:01:47.173
For the past 19 years

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.233
I've been working on yo-yo tricks,

00:01:49.233 --> 00:01:51.470
trying to figure out what tricks to do,

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:52.740
that's half the battle.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.990
(vibrant techno music)

00:01:58.186 --> 00:02:00.950
Because you're performing
those tricks to music,

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:03.774
one of the hardest
parts is telling a story

00:02:03.774 --> 00:02:06.398
through your music,
giving the right energy,

00:02:06.398 --> 00:02:09.231
and work on making something flow.

00:02:11.187 --> 00:02:12.990
It's a lotta hard work
that you put into it

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:16.073
and any split second of losing focus,

00:02:17.961 --> 00:02:22.654
it seems like a whole year's
of work goes to waste.

00:02:22.654 --> 00:02:26.142
I have to prove that I'm not
gonna waste the audience's time

00:02:26.142 --> 00:02:30.185
and for people to respond
positively towards it—

00:02:30.185 --> 00:02:31.987
(audience cheers loudly)

00:02:31.987 --> 00:02:34.883
That I like can't thank the sport enough.

00:02:34.883 --> 00:02:38.133
(vibrant techno music)

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.819
I started playing yo-yo
when I was four years old

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:44.642
and it's something I care about.

00:02:44.642 --> 00:02:47.724
It's not something I do for money.

00:02:47.724 --> 00:02:50.221
Like it's a toy, it's
a toy at simplest form,

00:02:50.221 --> 00:02:52.183
and I just happen to be competing

00:02:52.183 --> 00:02:53.762
with it for a really long time

00:02:53.762 --> 00:02:56.610
and spending a lot of time learning.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.818
In the end it's something that
makes me feel comfortable.

00:02:58.818 --> 00:03:00.354
It keeps me youthful.

00:03:00.354 --> 00:03:03.799
It reminds me of what I would
be playing with as a kid.

00:03:03.799 --> 00:03:07.049
(vibrant techno music)

00:03:12.137 --> 00:03:13.647
- [Voiceover] Good job.

00:03:13.647 --> 00:03:15.314
- [Voiceover] Oh,oh!

